-- title:
--   Local bijectivity of the period map over an affine open
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$, a ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{W}(p,\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to \mathbb{W}(p,k)$, and a formal $O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathbb{W}(p,k)/p$ which, for the structure map obtained from $\iota$ by reduction, is special (its Lie pieces in degrees $0$ and $1$ are complementary and invertible), has height $4$, and satisfies $\mathrm{lieZero} \subseteq \ker(\mathrm{lieVarpi})$. Let $M$ be a moduli package over $\mathbb{W}(p,k)$ that is a Zariski sheaf, let $\eta$ assign to every rigidified object over a ring $B$ with $p$ nilpotent a point of $M(B)$, and assume the three conditions of $\eta$: on Noetherian algebras it separates admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, it commutes with base change, and every point of $M(B)$ is, on a finite cover of $\operatorname{Spec} B$ by localisations away from elements generating the unit ideal, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$. Assume moreover that the degree-$0$ and degree-$1$ graded pieces of the Cartier module of $\Phi$ are complementary, that $r_\Phi : (\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to \mathbb{Z}_p) \to$ the associated $N$-module maps the whole source bijectively onto the degree-$0$ eta piece for every canonical $L$-map, and that $\theta$, assigning to points of $M(B)$ Deligne data over $B$ with uniformiser $p$, satisfies `IsPeriodMap`: it turns Cartier quadruples for admissible $t$ into Drinfeld quadruples for $\theta(\eta(t))$, and it commutes with base change. Finally let $Y$ be a reduced scheme with a separated morphism $\pi_Y$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{W}(p,k)/p)$ that is locally of finite type, together with bijections $e_Y$, natural in $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra maps compatible with the structure maps, between the $Y$-points over $\operatorname{Spec}\psi$ and the Deligne data over $B$, for Noetherian $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebras $B$ in which $p = 0$. Then for every affine open $V$ of $Y$ there are $n_0, m_0$ such that for all $n \ge n_0$, $m \ge m_0$, every Noetherian algebra $S$ over $\mathbb{W}(p,k)/p$ and over $\mathbb{Z}_p$ with $p$ nilpotent and $p = 0$, and every Deligne datum $d$ over $S$ whose corresponding $Y$-point has topological image contained in $V$, there is exactly one $x$ in $M(S)$ with $\theta(x) = d$ among those points of $M(S)$ admitting, on some finite cover of $\operatorname{Spec} S$ by localisations $L$ away from elements generating the unit ideal, an admissible rigidified object $t$ over $L$ with $t.n = n$, each coordinate of the series giving the action of $p^{n+m}$ on $\bar\Phi$ lying in the ideal generated by the coordinates of $t.\rho$, and $\eta(t)$ equal to the image of the point in $M(L)$.
--
--   This is the local form of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison: over each affine open of the special fibre of the $p$-adic upper half plane, the period map is a bijection from a sufficiently large bounded piece $M_{n,m}$ of the moduli package onto those Deligne data whose associated point lands in that open, as in Boutot–Carayol (12.3)–(12.5). It is the local input to the global bijectivity statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.ModuliPackage.IsPeriodMap.bijective_of_charP_of_isNoetherianRing_of_lieVarpi_eq_zero`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.ModuliPackage.IsPeriodMap.bijective_of_charP_of_isNoetherianRing_of_lieVarpi_eq_zero).
